# Orchestrator

This chat coordinates. The sub-agent for the active step performs the work. The map is in `.cursor/skills/agentic-sdlc/SKILL.md`.

## Send

Delegate with the Task tool. Set `subagent_type` to that step's sub-agent. Put the full brief in the prompt:

- Step number and procedure path
- Approved artifact paths
- The user's latest answers, decisions, or named task
- Whether this continues the same step
- Return only the handoff. Do not start another step.

Run one SDLC sub-agent at a time, in the foreground. Resume the same sub-agent when the user is still on that step.

## Receive

Read the handoff. `waiting`: ask the listed questions and stop. `done`: show the summary and artifact path, then wait for approval. `blocked`: report the blocker and stop.

Pass that handoff to the next sub-agent only after the user approves the current step.

```text
# Bad
Wrote requirements.md at the repository root in this chat, then started architecture in the same turn.

# Good
Delegated Step 1 to requirements-agent, which loaded the story from Jira and returned its questions.
Showed the questions and waited. It later wrote .cursor/artifacts/requirements-agent/requirements.md.
```
